---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import CtaBanner from "../components/CtaBanner.astro";
import NodeGraph from "../components/NodeGraph.astro";

const highlights = [
  {
    title: "Updates Go Live Instantly",
    body: "When the owner edits a photo or updates a service, the change shows up on the live site right away — no waiting on a developer, no delay, no extra step.",
  },
  {
    title: "A Simple Way to Manage Content",
    body: "We built a private control panel just for this business, covering services, project photos, testimonials, and the homepage slideshow. It only does what the owner actually needs — not a generic tool full of features he'll never touch.",
  },
  {
    title: "Reliable Hosting, Owned by the Client",
    body: "The site runs on hosting the owner controls directly, instead of renting space on a platform with its own recurring subscription — steady uptime, with no outside company that can change the deal later.",
  },
  {
    title: "Lead Capture Built In",
    body: "A contact form that emails the business directly and logs every submission, so no inquiry depends solely on an email server behaving.",
  },
];
---

<Layout
  title="How We Build: Elite Midwest Integrators"
  description="A detailed walkthrough of how SemanticKC approaches a build, illustrated by Elite Midwest Integrators — the technical decisions, the content-management setup, and the hosting choice, explained in plain terms."
>
  <section class="relative overflow-hidden px-4 py-20 text-center sm:px-6 sm:py-24 lg:px-8">
    <NodeGraph compact />
    <div class="relative mx-auto max-w-3xl">
      <p class="font-display mb-4 text-sm font-bold uppercase tracking-widest text-accent-300">How We Build</p>
      <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight text-white sm:text-5xl">
        Our Process, Walked Through One Real Build
      </h1>
      <p class="mx-auto mt-6 max-w-2xl text-lg text-white/65">
        This page isn't a portfolio grid — it's a detailed look at how we approach every engagement,
        using Elite Midwest Integrators, our first real client build, as the concrete example. As we
        take on more clients, more of these will get added here.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="px-4 pb-16 sm:px-6 sm:pb-20 lg:px-8">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl rounded-3xl border border-line bg-card px-6 py-10 sm:px-10">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-white sm:text-3xl">The Situation</h2>
      <p class="mt-5 leading-relaxed text-white/65">
        Elite Midwest Integrators needed a site that would build trust with commercial clients
        evaluating a security/network systems vendor, generate quote requests, and let the owner
        update project photos, testimonials, and service listings without going through a developer
        for every small change.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="px-4 pb-16 sm:px-6 sm:pb-20 lg:px-8">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-5xl">
      <h2 class="mb-10 text-center text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-white sm:text-3xl">
        What Was Built
      </h2>
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 gap-5 sm:grid-cols-2">
        {highlights.map((h) => (
          <div class="min-w-0 rounded-2xl border border-line bg-card p-6">
            <h3 class="font-bold text-white">{h.title}</h3>
            <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-white/60">{h.body}</p>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="px-4 pb-16 sm:px-6 sm:pb-20 lg:px-8">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl rounded-3xl border border-line bg-card px-6 py-10 sm:px-10">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-white sm:text-3xl">Why This Approach</h2>
      <p class="mt-5 leading-relaxed text-white/65">
        This is the same team and process building SemanticKC's own site — the difference is that
        Elite Midwest Integrators is a non-technical client who needed to run day-to-day content
        updates themselves, which is why that build includes a full content-management panel and
        this one deliberately doesn't. The right setup depends on who's maintaining the site day to
        day, not on defaulting to the same approach every time.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-5 leading-relaxed text-white/65">
        <!-- DRAFT: no outcome metrics (traffic, leads, conversion) are listed
             here — we haven't fabricated numbers, and real figures should
             only go in once Sean confirms what's shareable. -->
        We're intentionally not listing traffic or lead numbers here — this section describes the
        build itself, not results, until there are real, confirmed figures worth sharing.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-5 leading-relaxed text-white/65">
        <!-- Case-study framing note: this is currently our one completed
             client build. This page is written to walk through our
             methodology using that build as a concrete example, rather
             than presenting it as one entry in a larger portfolio we
             don't yet have — see the intro above the case study for the
             explicit framing. -->
        Elite Midwest Integrators is our first client build, and right now our only one — we're not
        going to pad this page with work we haven't actually done. What we can show you is exactly
        how we think through a build, start to finish, with a real example instead of a hypothetical.
        That's the point of this page.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <CtaBanner
    heading="Want a site built the same way?"
    subheading="Every engagement starts with a conversation about what your business actually needs."
  />
</Layout>
